hadiths[226]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2507","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Rejoice, 'Ammar! The transgressing group will kill you."
"2508","On the authority of Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith: She entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I saw a terrible dream last night."" He said: ""What is it?"" She said: ""It is severe."" He said: ""What is it?"" She said: ""I saw as if a piece of your body was cut off and placed in my lap."" He said: ""You have seen good. Fatimah will give birth, if Allah wills, to a boy who will be in your lap."" So Fatimah gave birth to al-Husayn, and he was in my lap just as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. Then I entered one day upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and placed him in his lap. Then I glanced away for a moment, and behold, the eyes of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were flowing with tears. She said: I said: ""O Prophet of Allah! May my father and mother be ransomed for you, what is the matter with you?"" He said: ""Jibril came to me, peace be upon him, and informed me that my ummah will kill this son of mine."" I said: ""This one?"" He said: ""Yes, and he brought me some reddish soil from his soil."""
"2509","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah bin 'Amr, from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) who said: ""Leave the Abyssinians alone as long as they leave you alone, for no one will extract the treasure of the Ka'bah except Dhu al-Suwayqatayn from the Abyssinians."
"2510","[AI-translation] Asqa' who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) came out to us and said: ""Do you claim that I will be the last of you to die? No, I am the first of you to die, and you will follow me in groups, destroying one another."
"2511","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: When Allah gathers the former and the latter on the Day of Resurrection, the Lord, Blessed and Exalted is He, will come to the believers, and He will stop before them while the believers are upon a mound. They said: ""What is the mound?"" He said: ""An elevated place."" He will say: ""Do you recognize your Lord?"" They will say: ""If He introduces Himself to us, we will recognize Him."" Then He will say to them a second time, and He will smile in their faces, so they will fall down before Him in prostration."
"2512","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When Allah gathers the servants on a single plain, a caller will call out: 'Let every people follow what they used to worship.' So every people will follow what they used to worship, and the people will remain in their state. Then He will come to them and say: 'What is the matter with the people that they have gone and you are here?' They will say: 'We are waiting for our Lord.' He will say: 'Do you recognize Him?' They will say: 'If He reveals Himself to us, we will recognize Him.' Then He will uncover His shin for them, and they will fall down in prostration. And that is the saying of Allah the Exalted: 'On the Day when the Shin shall be uncovered, and they shall be called to prostrate, but they shall not be able' (Al-Qalam: 42). And every hypocrite will remain, unable to prostrate. Then He will lead them to Paradise."""
"2513","On the authority of ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat in a gathering of his, and Jibrīl عليه السلام came to him and sat before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, placing his hands on the knees of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Inform me, what is Islam?"" (I said: So he mentioned the ḥadīth in its entirety, and in it) he said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Then inform me, when is the Hour?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Glory be to Allah! It is among five things of the unseen that none knows except Him: 'Indeed, Allah [alone] has knowledge of the Hour' (Luqmān: 34). But if you wish, I will inform you of its portents before that."" He said: ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah! Then inform me."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""When you see the slave-girl giving birth to her mistress—or her master—and you see the herdsmen of sheep competing in constructing buildings, and you see the barefoot, naked, destitute shepherds becoming the leaders of people, then that is among the portents of the Hour and its signs."" He said: ""O Messenger of Allah! And who are the herdsmen of sheep and the barefoot, naked, destitute?"" He said: ""The Arabs."""
"2514","[AI-translation] Narrated Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, raised (mursal): If you adorn your mosques and decorate your copies of the Quran, then destruction is upon you."
"2515","[AI-translation] Qa'qa' ibn Abi Hadrad al-Aslami: She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, upon the pulpit saying: O people! If you hear of an army that has been swallowed up nearby, then the Hour has cast its shadow."
"2516","[AI-translation] Narrated Aishah, attributing it to the Prophet, peace be upon him: When evil appears in the land, Allah sends down His punishment upon the people of the land. She (Aishah) said: ""Even if among them are people who obey Allah, Mighty and Majestic?"" He said: ""Yes, then they will return to the mercy of Allah, Exalted is He."
"2517","[AI-translation] Narrated Aishah, raised to the Prophet: When evil appears in the land, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sends down His punishment upon the people of the land. And if among them are righteous people, they will be afflicted with what afflicts the people, then they will return to the mercy of Allah."
"2518","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: When a man says, ""The people are ruined,"" he is the most ruined of them."
"2519","[AI-translation] Ash'ari) from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, he said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, an angel will be sent to every believer with a disbeliever with him, and the angel will say to the believer: O believer! Here is this disbeliever, for this is your ransom from the Fire."
"2520","[AI-translation] Miqdad: He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: When the Day of Resurrection comes, the sun will be brought near to the servants until it is a mile or two away. The sun will scorch them, and they will be in sweat according to their deeds. Among them are those whom it will take up to their ankles, among them are those whom it will take up to their knees, among them are those whom it will take up to their waists, and among them are those whom it will bridle with a bridle. I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, indicating with his hand to his mouth, meaning it will bridle him with a bridle."
"2521","[AI-translation] Narrated Udaysah bint Uhbān: She said: When Ali ibn Abi Talib came here (to Basrah), he entered upon my father and said: O Abu Muslim, will you not help me against these people? He said: Yes. He said: He called a slave girl of his and said: O girl! Bring out my sword. She brought it out, and he drew from it about a span, and it was wood! He said: My close friend and your cousin advised me: If there is a civil war among the Muslims, then take a sword of wood. If you wish, I will go out with you. He (Ali) said: I have no need for you or your sword."
"2522","[AI-translation] Narrated Abdullah ibn Umar: He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: When my nation walks with the boastful gait and its servants are the sons of kings, the sons of Persia and Rome, the evil among them will be given authority over the good among them."
"2523","[AI-translation] From 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""Tonight I was shown at the Ka'bah, and I saw a man of dark complexion, the most handsome of men of dark complexion you could see, with hair reaching his shoulders, the most handsome of shoulder-length hair you could see, which he had combed and it was dripping water, leaning on two men or on the shoulders of two men, circumambulating the Ka'bah. I asked, 'Who is this?' It was said, 'This is the Masih, son of Maryam.' Then I saw a man with tightly curled hair, whose right eye was blind as if it were a floating grape. I asked, 'Who is this?' It was said to me, 'This is the Masih, the Dajjal.'"
"2524","[AI-translation] Nadr ibn Anas ibn Malik from his father who said: I asked the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, to intercede for me on the Day of Resurrection. He said: ""I will do so."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Where shall I look for you?"" He said: ""Look for me, the first place you look for me, at the Sirat."" I said: ""If I do not meet you at the Sirat?"" He said: ""Look for me at the Mizan."" I said: ""If I do not meet you at the Mizan?"" He said: ""Then look for me at the Hawd, for I will not miss these three locations."
"2525","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: ""Trials will overshadow you like the dark patches of the night. The most saved of people from them will be the owner of a mountain peak who eats from the milk of his sheep, or a man beyond the frontier posts holding the reins of his horse, eating from the spoils of his sword."
"2526","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, marfu'an: The Jews split into seventy-one or seventy-two sects, and the Christians split into seventy-one or seventy-two sects, and my Ummah will split into seventy-three sects."
"2527","[AI-translation] From Ibn Mas'ud, marfu'an: ""The Hour has drawn near, and the people will only increase in greed for the world, and they will only increase in distance from Allah."
"2528","[AI-translation] From Abu Musa from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: ""Break your bows — meaning during the fitnah — and cut your bowstrings, and stay in the interiors of the houses, and be in them like the best of the sons of Adam."
"2529","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar, marfu'an: ""Verily, the fitnah is here, verily, the fitnah is here"" — he said it two or three times — ""from where the horn of Satan rises"" (he pointed with his hand towards the East, and in a narration: towards Iraq)."
"2530","[AI-translation] The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Verily, the fitnah is here, from where the horn of Satan rises."" This is from the hadith of Ibn 'Umar, Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, Ibn 'Abbas, and Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with them."
"2531","[AI-translation] From Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan that he stood among us and said: ""Verily, the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, stood among us and said: 'Verily, those before you of the People of the Book split into seventy-two sects, and this religion will split into seventy-three: seventy-two in the Fire and one in Paradise, and it is the Jama'ah.'"
"2532","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, appointed a man over a task. He said: ""O Messenger of Allah, choose for me."" He said: ""Stay in your house."
"2533","[AI-translation] From Abdullah that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, supplicated and said: ""O Allah, bless us in our Makkah. O Allah, bless us in our Madinah. O Allah, bless us in our Sham, and bless us in our Saa', and bless us in our Mudd."" A man said: ""O Messenger of Allah! And in our Iraq?"" So he turned away from him. He repeated it three times, each time the man saying: ""And in our Iraq,"" and he turning away from him. He then said: ""Therein are earthquakes and trials, and therein will rise the horn of Satan."
"2534","[AI-translation] From Qatada: Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to us: A man said: ""O Prophet of Allah! Will the disbeliever be resurrected on his face on the Day of Resurrection?"" He said: ""Is not the One who made him walk on two legs in this world capable of making him walk on his face on the Day of Resurrection?"" Qatada said: ""Yes, by the might of our Lord."
"2535","[AI-translation] From Anas, he said: The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, passed by a people afflicted with illness, and said: ""Did these not ask for well-being?"
"2536","[AI-translation] From Abu Musa he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""My nation is a merciful nation; there is no punishment upon it in the Hereafter. Its punishment in this world is trials, earthquakes, and volcanoes."
"2537","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik, he said: The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""Indeed, a man will intercede for two and three, and a man for a man."
"2538","[AI-translation] From Shaddad bin Aws, raised to the Prophet: ""Indeed, Allah gathered the earth for me, and I saw its easts and wests, and indeed the dominion of my nation will reach what was gathered for me of it."
"2539","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Allah will single out a man from my Ummah before all creation on the Day of Resurrection, and He will spread out ninety-nine scrolls for him, each scroll as far as the eye can see. Then He will say: 'Do you deny any of this? Have My recording angels wronged you?' He will say: 'No, O Lord!' He will say: 'Do you have any excuse?' He will say: 'No, O Lord!' He will say: 'Rather, you have a good deed with Us, and you shall not be wronged today.' Then a card will be brought out containing: 'I bear witness that there is no deity but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.' He will say: 'Bring your weight.' He will say: 'What is this card compared to these scrolls?' He said: 'You shall not be wronged.' He said: 'The scrolls will be placed in one pan of the scale, and the card in the other pan. The scrolls will fly up (become light), and the card will weigh heavy. For nothing weighs heavy with the Name of Allah.'"""
"2540","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik, raised to the Prophet: ""Indeed, Allah does not wrong a believer for a good deed; he is given reward for it (and in a narration: he is rewarded for it in this world) and is recompensed for it in the Hereafter. As for the disbeliever, he is fed with the good deeds he did for the sake of Allah in this world until when he arrives in the Hereafter, he has no good deed for which to be recompensed."
"2541","[AI-translation] From Abu Huraira he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Indeed, Allah will send a wind from Yemen softer than silk, and it will not leave anyone in whose heart is the weight of a grain of faith except that it will seize him."
"2542","[AI-translation] Khudri who says: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: ""Indeed, Allah will question the servant on the Day of Resurrection until He says: 'What prevented you when you saw the evil from denouncing it?' So when Allah grants a servant his argument, he will say: 'O my Lord! I trusted in You and feared the people.'"
"2543","[AI-translation] From Aisha she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: ""Indeed, the first thing to be overturned."" Meaning Islam: ""is overturned like,"" meaning wine. It was said: ""How, O Messenger of Allah, when Allah has clarified regarding it what He clarified?"" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""They will call it by other than its name."
"2544","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""Indeed, for the one who lies about me, a house will be built for him in the Fire."
"2545","[AI-translation] From Anas, raised to the Prophet: ""Indeed, Allah has withheld repentance from the companion of every innovation."
"2546","[AI-translation] Ibn 'Abbas narrated from the Prophet (peace be upon him), he said: ""The affair of this Ummah will not cease to be near or agreeable until they speak about the children and Qadar."
"2547","[AI-translation] From Khabbab, from the Prophet (peace be upon him), who said: ""When the Children of Israel perished, they narrated stories."
"2548","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: ""Indeed, Islam has a fervor, and every fervor has a lapse. So if its companion is upright and moderate, then hope for him; but if he is pointed to with fingers, then do not hope for him."
"2549","[AI-translation] From Haram bin Hakim, from his uncle 'Abdullah bin Sa'd, from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), who said: ""You are in a time when its jurists are many, its preachers are few, its askers are few, its givers are many, and action in it is better than knowledge. But there will come a time when its jurists are few, its preachers are many, its askers are many, its givers are few, and knowledge in it is better than action."
"2550","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: ""Knowledge is only acquired through learning, and forbearance is only acquired through practicing forbearance. Whoever seeks good is given it, and whoever guards against evil is protected from it."
"2551","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar, raised to the Prophet: ""The parable of the companion of the Qur'an is like the companion of tethered camels: if he watches over them, he retains them, and if he lets them loose, they depart."
"2552","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah bin 'Amr, he said: I went early in the morning to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) one day. He said: He heard the voices of two men disputing over a verse, so the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) came out to us, with anger recognizable on his face, and said: ""Those before you were only destroyed because of their disagreements concerning the Book."
"2553","Abdur-Rahman bin Abd Rabb al-Ka'bah said: I entered the mosque and found Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As sitting in the shade of the Ka'bah, with people gathered around him. I came to them and sat with him. He said: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, so we alighted at a stopping place. Some of us were setting up their tents, some were shooting arrows, and some were tending to their beasts. Then the caller of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced: ""Prayer is a gathering."" So we gathered around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: ""There was no prophet before me but it was incumbent upon him to guide his nation to the best of what he knew for them and to warn them against the worst of what he knew for them. And your nation, its well-being has been placed in its first part, and its last part will be afflicted with calamities and things you will deny. A trial (fitnah) will come, making some of it follow others. A trial will come and the believer will say: 'This is my destruction.' Then it will be lifted. A trial will come and the believer will say: 'This is it, this is it.' So whoever wishes to be removed from the Fire and admitted into Paradise, let death come to him while he believes in Allah and the Last Day, and let him treat people as he would love to be treated. And whoever pledges allegiance to an Imam, giving him the clasp of his hand and the fruit of his heart, let him obey him as long as he is able. If another comes to dispute with him, strike the neck of the other.""He added at the end: I drew close to him and said to him: ""I adjure you by Allah, did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"" He pointed to his ears and his heart with his hands and said: ""My ears heard it and my heart retained it."" I said to him: ""This cousin of yours, Mu'awiyah, orders us to consume our wealth among ourselves unjustly and to kill ourselves, while Allah says: [And do not consume one another's wealth unjustly... and do not kill yourselves...] (An-Nisa)."" He remained silent for a while, then said: ""Obey him in obedience to Allah, and disobey him in disobedience to Allah."""
"2554","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace be upon him): ""Allah has one hundred mercies. He has distributed one mercy among the people of the world, sufficing them until their appointed terms, and has kept ninety-nine mercies for His allies. And Allah will take that mercy which He distributed among the people of the world and add it to the ninety-nine, completing them to one hundred mercies for His allies on the Day of Resurrection."
"2555","[AI-translation] Khudri, marfu'an: ""Indeed, I have a reservoir between the Ka'bah and Bayt al-Maqdis, white like milk. Its vessels are as numerous as the stars. And indeed, I am the Prophet with the most followers on the Day of Resurrection."
"2556","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Rib'i bin Hirash who said: 'Uqbah bin 'Amr said to Hudhayfah: ""Will you not tell us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him?"" He said: ""I heard him say: 'With the Dajjal, when he emerges, will be water and fire. As for that which the people see as fire, it is cold water; and as for that which the people see as cold water, it is a burning fire. So whoever among you reaches that, let him fall into that which he sees as fire, for it is sweet and cold.'"" 'Uqbah said: ""And I have heard it,"" in confirmation of Hudhayfah."
"2557","From Al-Aswad ibn Yazid, who said: The prayer was established in the mosque, so we came walking with Abdullah ibn Mas'ud. When the people bowed, Abdullah bowed and we bowed with him while still walking. A man passed in front of him and said: ""Peace be upon you, O Abu Abdur-Rahman!"" Abdullah said while bowing: ""Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth."" When he finished the prayer, some of the people asked him: ""Why did you say, when the man greeted you, 'Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth'?"" He said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: 'Indeed, among the portents of the Hour is that the greeting is given only on the basis of acquaintance.' In another narration: 'That a man greets a man only because of acquaintance.'"""
"2558","[AI-translation] It was narrated from 'Amr bin Taghlab who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Among the signs of the Hour is that wealth will abound, ignorance will increase, tribulations will appear, and trade will spread (and knowledge will appear)."
"2559","[AI-translation] Jumahi that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""Among the signs of the Hour is that knowledge will be sought from the younger ones."
"2560","[AI-translation] It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud, marfu'an: ""Among the signs of the Hour is that a man will pass through the mosque without praying two rak'ahs in it."
"2561","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Anas bin Malik, marfu'an: ""Among the signs of the Hour are obscenity and its open display, the severing of ties of kinship, and entrusting the betrayer—I think he said: and distrusting the trustworthy."
"2562","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Abu Qilabah who said: I saw a man in Madinah, and the people were gathered around him while he was saying: ""The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said... The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said."" Then a man from the Companions of the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""I heard him saying: 'After you will come the lying misguider, and at his head after him will be deceit, deceit,' three times. 'And he will say: ""I am your Lord."" So whoever says: ""You are not our Lord, rather our Lord is Allah, upon Him we rely, and to Him we turn. I seek refuge in Allah from your evil,"" he will have no authority over him.'"
"2563","[AI-translation] It was narrated from 'Utbah bin Ghazwan, the brother of Banu Mazin bin Sa'sa'ah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Ahead of you are the days of patience. For the one who adheres during those days to what you are upon, the reward of fifty of you will be recorded."" They said: ""O Prophet of Allah! From them?"" He said: ""Rather, from you."
"2564","[AI-translation] Khudri that when death approached him, he called for new clothes and wore them, then said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: 'The deceased will be resurrected in the clothes he dies in.'"
"2565","On the authority of Abu Hurayrah, attributed to the Prophet: Verily, Gog and Magog dig every day until, when they almost see the rays of the sun, the one in charge of them says: ""Return, for we will dig it tomorrow."" Then Allah restores it stronger than before. This continues until their appointed term arrives and Allah wills to send them against the people. They dig until, when they almost see the rays of the sun, the one in charge of them says: ""Return, for we will dig it tomorrow, if Allah wills,"" and they make the exception. So they return to it and find it as they left it. They then dig through it and emerge upon the people. They drink up the waters, and the people take refuge in their fortresses. They shoot their arrows into the sky, and the arrows return stained with clotted blood. They say: ""We have conquered the people of earth and prevailed over the people of heaven."" Then Allah sends a worm (or insect) into their necks, and they are killed by it. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the beasts of the earth will grow fat and give thanks from their flesh."""
"2566","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Anas bin Malik: A man asked the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him: ""When will the Hour be established?"" And with him was a young boy from the Ansar named Muhammad. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said to him: ""If this boy lives, perhaps he will not reach old age before the Hour is established."
"2567","Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah al-Dawsi said: I and a companion of mine entered upon a man from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We said: ""Narrate to us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and do not narrate to us from anyone other than him, even if he is trustworthy in our view."" He said: ""Yes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us one day and said: 'I warn you of the Dajjal, I warn you of the Dajjal, I warn you of the Dajjal. For there has been no prophet but he warned his nation of him. And he is among you, O nation. And he is curly-haired, dark-skinned, with his left eye obliterated (blind). And with him are a Paradise and a Fire; his Fire is a Paradise and his Paradise is a Fire. And with him are a river of water and a mountain of bread. And he will be empowered over a person, so he will kill him, then bring him back to life; he will not be empowered over anyone else. And he will command the sky to rain, and it will rain, and the earth to bring forth vegetation, but it will not bring forth. And he will remain on the earth for forty mornings, until he reaches every watering place (or pass) of it. And he will not approach four mosques: the Sacred Mosque, the Mosque of the Messenger, the Mosque of Jerusalem, and Mount Tur. And whatever of things becomes ambiguous to you, then verily Allah is not one-eyed (repeated twice).'"""
"2568","[AI-translation] Musa ibn Uqba said: My grandfather, the father of my mother, Abu Habiba, narrated to me: He entered the house while Uthman was besieged therein, and he heard Abu Hurayra seeking permission from Uthman to speak. He granted him permission, so he stood, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: 'You will encounter after me trial and discord,' or he said, 'discord and trial.' A speaker from the people said: 'Then who is for us, O Messenger of Allah?!' He said: 'Stick to the trustworthy one and his companions,' and he pointed to Uthman with that."
"2569","[AI-translation] From Bahz ibn Hakim ibn Muawiya, from his father, from his grandfather (Muawiya ibn Hayda), marfu'an: You will be summoned (on the Day of Resurrection) with your mouths muzzled with the fidam. Then the first thing that will speak (he said once: interpret, and in a narration: articulate) on behalf of one of you will be his thigh and his hand."
"2570","[AI-translation] From Abu Dharr, marfu'an: You are today in a time whose scholars are many and whose preachers are few. Whoever abandons a tenth of what he knows has strayed. And there will come after that a time whose preachers are many and whose scholars are few. Whoever holds fast to a tenth of what he knows will be saved."
"2571","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayra, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace be upon him: The great, corpulent man will come on the Day of Resurrection not weighing with Allah the wing of a mosquito. And he said: ""Recite: So We will not assign for them any weight on the Day of Resurrection (105) (Al-Kahf)."
"2572","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Rafi', the freed slave of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him), that she said: ""I used to hear the people mentioning the Pool (Al-Hawd), but I did not hear that from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). Then, one day, while a servant girl was combing my hair, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) saying: 'O people!' I said to the servant girl: 'Move away from me.' She said: 'He only called the men; he did not call the women.' I said: 'I am among the people.' The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: 'I am your precursor at the Pool, so beware! Let none of you come to me and be driven away from me as a stray camel is driven away, so that I say: ""What is the matter with this?"" And it is said: ""You do not know what they innovated after you."" So I say: ""Away with them! Away with them!""'"""
"2573","On the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās, from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""I am holding you back from the Fire by your waist-wrappers, yet you rush into it like moths and locusts. Soon I shall let go of your waist-wrappers, and I shall be your predecessor at the Basin; you will come to me in groups and scattered, and I shall recognize you by your names and your marks, just as a man recognizes his stray camel among his camels. Then a group will be driven to the left, and I shall plead for you to the Lord of the Worlds, saying: 'O Lord, my Ummah!' It will be said: 'You do not know what they innovated after you; they kept turning back on their heels after you.' So I shall not recognize any of you who comes on the Day of Resurrection carrying a sheep bleating, calling: 'O Muḥammad! O Muḥammad!' I shall say: 'I cannot avail you anything against Allah; I have conveyed the message.' And I shall not recognize any of you who comes on the Day of Resurrection carrying a camel grunting, calling: 'O Muḥammad! O Muḥammad!' I shall say: 'I cannot avail you anything against Allah; I have conveyed.' And I shall not recognize any of you who comes on the Day of Resurrection carrying a horse neighing, calling: 'O Muḥammad! O Muḥammad!' I shall say: 'I cannot avail you anything against Allah; I have conveyed.' And I shall not recognize any of you who comes on the Day of Resurrection carrying a piece of leather, calling: 'O Muḥammad! O Muḥammad!' I shall say: 'I cannot avail you anything against Allah; I have conveyed.'"""
"2574","[AI-translation] From Abu Umama from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: The first of the signs is the rising of the sun from its west."
"2575","[AI-translation] Aswad al-Anasi narrated to him: He came to Ubada ibn al-Samit while he was staying on the coast of Homs in a building of his, and with him was Umm Haram. Umayr said: Umm Haram narrated to us that she heard the Prophet, peace be upon him, say: ""The first army of my Ummah to raid the sea have earned their reward."" Umm Haram said: I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Am I among them?"" He said: ""You are among them."" Then he said: ""The first army of my Ummah to raid the city of Caesar are forgiven."" I said: ""Am I among them, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""No."
"2576","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayra that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: The first to be summoned on the Day of Resurrection is Adam, so his progeny will appear to him. It will be said: ""This is your father Adam."" He will say: ""Labbayka wa sa'dayk!"" He will say: ""Bring out the contingent of Hell from your progeny."" He will say: ""O Lord! How many do I bring out?"" He will say: ""Bring out from every hundred, ninety-nine."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah! If there are taken from us from every hundred ninety-nine, then what remains of us?"" He said: ""My Ummah among the nations is like the white hair in the black bull."
"2577","[AI-translation] From Abu Dharr that he said to Yazid ibn Abi Sufyan: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: The first to change my Sunnah is a man from Banu Umayya."
"2578","[AI-translation] From Aisha, marfu'an: The first to be clothed is the Khalil of Allah, Ibrahim, upon him be prayers and peace."
"2579","[AI-translation] From Qays ibn Abi Hazim: That Aisha said when she reached al-Haw'ab she heard the barking of dogs, so she said: I do not think myself to be anything but returning, for the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said to us: ""Which of you will have the dogs of al-Haw'ab bark at her?"" Al-Zubayr said to her: ""Will you return? Perhaps Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will reconcile between the people through you."
"2580","[AI-translation] 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""The signs are like beads strung on a thread; if the thread is cut, they follow one another."
"2581","From ʿAlim, who said: I was with ʿAbis al-Ghifārī on a roof when he saw some people fleeing from the plague. He said: ""What is with these people fleeing from the plague?! O plague! Take me to you (twice)."" His cousin, a Companion, said to him: ""Why do you wish for death when I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Let none of you wish for death, for when he dies his deeds come to an end, (and he is not returned to make amends).'"" He said: ""Hasten to perform deeds before six characteristics appear: the rule of fools, the abundance of police, the severing of family ties, the selling of judgments, the taking of blood lightly, and a people who take the Quran as psalms, putting forward a man who is not the most knowledgeable among them nor the most learned; they put him forward only to sing for them."""
"2582","[AI-translation] Abu Hurayrah reported from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, that he said: ""Hasten to perform deeds before six things: the rising of the sun from its west, the Dajjal, the smoke, the beast of the earth, the death of one of you, and the general affair."
"2583","[AI-translation] Abu Hurayrah reported it as marfu': ""Hasten to perform deeds before trials like the pieces of a dark night; a man becomes a believer in the morning and a disbeliever in the evening, or a believer in the evening and a disbeliever in the morning, selling his religion for a portion of the world."
"2584","[AI-translation] Ashja'i Sa'd ibn Tariq (ibn Ashim) reported from his father that he heard the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, saying: ""Sufficient for my companions is killing."
"2585","[AI-translation] Abu Jubayrah reported it as marfu': ""I was sent in the breath of the Hour."
"2586","[AI-translation] Sa'idi reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""I and the Hour were sent like these two,"" and he joined his middle finger and the one next to the thumb. He then said: ""The likeness of me and the Hour is only like two racing horses."" Then he said: ""The likeness of me and the Hour is only like the likeness of a man sent by his people as a scout, and when he feared being overtaken, he gestured with his garment: 'You have come, you have come! I am that, I am that!'"
"2587","[AI-translation] The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Before the Hour, you will fight a people whose shoes are of hair."" And he said: ""This is al-Bariz."" And Sufyan said one time: ""They are the people of al-Bazir."
"2588","[AI-translation] 'Abd Allah reported from the Prophet, peace be upon him: ""Before the Hour there will be transformation, sinking, and stoning."
"2589","[AI-translation] Ibn Mas'ud reported from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: ""Before the Hour, usury, fornication, and wine will appear."
"2590","[AI-translation] Abu Hurayrah reported from the Prophet, peace be upon him: ""While I was asleep, the treasures of the earth were brought to me, and two gold bracelets were placed in my hands. They grew heavy upon me and worried me, so it was revealed to me: 'Blow them off.' I blew them off and they vanished. I interpreted them as the two liars between whom I am: the master of San'a and the master of al-Yamamah."
"2591","[AI-translation] From 'Ayyash bin Abi Rabi'ah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, say: A wind will emerge before the Hour in which the souls of every believer will be taken."
"2592","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah, raising it to the Prophet, peace be upon him: The Beast will emerge and brand the people on their noses, then they will live long among you until a man buys a camel and says: From whom did you buy it? He says: I bought it from one of the branded ones."
"2593","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud, raised to the Prophet: The mill of Islam will turn after thirty-five, or thirty-six, or thirty-seven. If they perish, it is the way of those who perished, and if their religion stands for them, it will stand for them for seventy years. I said: (And in a narration: 'Umar said: O Prophet of Allah!) Is that of what remains or of what has passed? He said: Of what has passed."
"2594","[AI-translation] Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him: Dates or ripe dates were presented to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, and they ate from them until they left nothing but pits and what has no good in it. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Do you know what this is? You will take away the good upon good until there remains none of you like this —and he pointed to a pit— and what has no good in it."
"2595","[AI-translation] Ansari, that some of the Companions of the Prophet informed him that the Prophet said that day while warning them of his trial (meaning: the Dajjal): Know that none of you will see his Lord until he dies, and it is written between his eyes (K F R), which he who hates his deed will read."
"2596","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, say: Seek refuge in Allah from the head of the seventies and the leadership of boys."
"2597","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: The earth will throw up pieces of its liver like pillars of gold and silver. The killer will come and say: For this I killed. And the severer of kinship ties will come and say: For this I severed my kinship. And the thief will come and say: For this my hand was cut off. Then they will leave it, not taking anything from it."
"2598","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik, raised to the Prophet: There will be trials before the Hour like pieces of a dark night, in which a man will wake up a believer and go to bed an unbeliever, and go to bed a believer and wake up an unbeliever; people will sell their religion for worldly goods."
"2599","On the authority of ʿAmr ibn Wābiṣah al-Asadī from his father, who said: I was in Kufa in my house when I heard at the door of the house: ""Peace be upon you, may I enter?"" I said: ""And upon you be peace, enter."" When he entered, it was ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd. I said: ""O Abū ʿAbdur-Raḥmān! What hour of visitation is this?"" And that was at the height of midday. He said: ""The day became long for me, so I remembered whom I could converse with."" He said: So he began narrating to me about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I narrated to him. Then he began narrating to me. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ""There will be a tribulation in which the sleeper is better than the one lying down, and the one lying down is better than the one sitting, and the one sitting is better than the one standing, and the one standing is better than the one walking, and the one walking is better than the one riding, and the one riding is better than the one running. All its killed ones are in the Fire."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! And when is that?"" He said: ""That is during the days of Harj (killing/chaos)."" I said: ""And when are the days of Harj?"" He said: ""When a man does not feel safe from his companion."" I said: ""What do you command me if I reach that time?"" He said: ""Restrain yourself and your hand, and enter your house."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! What if someone enters upon me in my house?"" He said: ""Then enter your room."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! What if someone enters upon me in my room?"" He said: ""Then enter your mosque, and do thus""—and he grasped his right hand on his elbow—""and say: My Lord is Allah, until you die upon that."""
"2600","From Subay', who said: They sent me from Ma' to Kufa to purchase mounts. We came to the Kunasa (market), and there was a man surrounded by a crowd. My companion went to the mounts, while I approached him and found it was Hudhayfa. I heard him saying: ""The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to ask him about good, but I used to ask him about evil. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, will there be evil after this good, just as there was evil before it?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'Then what is the protection from it?' He said: 'The sword, I think.' I said: 'Then what?' He said: 'Then there will be a truce on a dubious basis (dakhan), then there will be callers to misguidance.' He said: 'If you see on that day the Caliph of Allah on earth, then cling to him, even if he exhausts your body and takes your wealth. If you do not see him, then flee in the earth, even if you die while clinging to the root of a tree.' I said: 'Then what?' He said: 'Then the Dajjal will emerge...' — the hadith continues."
"2601","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, who said: Three, when they emerge, no soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or earned good in its faith (158) (Al-An'am: 158): the rising of the sun from its west, the Dajjal, and the Beast of the Earth."
"2602","[AI-translation] From 'Adi bin Zaid, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, protected every side of Madinah by a barid by a barid; its trees will not be beaten nor cut, except what is used to drive the camel."
"2603","[AI-translation] From Thawban, raised to the Prophet: My Basin is between Aden and Oman. Its water is whiter than snow and sweeter than honey. The most numerous of people to come to it will be the poor Emigrants, with dishevelled hair, dirty clothes, who do not marry the pampered women, and for whom doors are not opened, who give the rights incumbent upon them and do not demand the rights due to them."
"2604","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), who said: The signs will emerge one upon the heels of another, following each other like beads on a string."
"2605","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas, raised to the Prophet: The Dajjal is one-eyed, reddish-white, bright (in a narration: bright as the moon), as if his head is a snake, the most similar of people to Abd al-Uzza bin Qatan. So if he perishes, perish he will, for verily your Lord, the Exalted, is not one-eyed."
"2606","[AI-translation] From Ubayy bin Kab, raised to the Prophet: The Dajjal's eye is green like glass, and we seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of the grave."
"2607","[AI-translation] From Muadh bin Jabal, raised to the Prophet: Six are from the signs of the Hour: my death, the conquest of Bayt al-Maqdis, a death that takes among the people like the sudden death of sheep, a trial whose heat enters the house of every Muslim, that a man will be given a thousand dinars and will be displeased with it, and that the Romans will break their pledge and march in eighty banners, under each banner twelve thousand."
"2608","[AI-translation] From Abdullah bin Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: A fire will emerge before the Day of Resurrection from the sea of Hadramawt, gathering the people. They said: O Messenger of Allah! What do you command us? He said: Upon you is Sham."
"2609","[AI-translation] From Abu Juhayfah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: The world will be opened up to you until the Kabah is adorned. We said: And we will be upon our religion today? He said: And you will be upon your religion today. We said: So will we be better then or today? He said: Rather, you are better today."
"2610","[AI-translation] From a man of Banu Sulaym, from his grandfather, that he came to the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) with some silver. He said: This is from a mine of ours. So the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: There will be mines attended by the worst of people."
"2611","[AI-translation] As, raised to the Prophet: There will be migration after migration. The best of the people of the earth will adhere to the migration of Ibrahim, and the worst of its people will remain in the earth. Their land will spew them out, the soul of Allah will detest them, and the Fire will gather them with the monkeys and swine."
"2612","From Anas: That Abdullah ibn Salam came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) upon his arrival in Medina and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I am going to ask you about three things which none knows except a Prophet."" He said: ""Ask."" He said: ""What is the first of the signs of the Hour? And what is the first thing that the people of Paradise will eat? And from where does the child resemble his father and his mother?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Gabriel has just informed me of them."" He said: ""That is the enemy of the Jews among the angels!"" He said: ""As for the first of the signs of the Hour, it is a fire that will emerge from the East and gather the people to the West. And as for the first thing that the people of Paradise will eat, it is the extra lobe of the fish's liver. And as for the resemblance of the child to his father and mother: if the man's fluid precedes the woman's fluid, the child will resemble him, and if the woman's fluid precedes the man's fluid, the child will resemble her."" He said: ""I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah."" And he said: ""O Messenger of Allah! The Jews are a people of falsehood, and if they learn of my Islam before you ask them about me, they will slander me to you. So send for them and ask them about me: what kind of man is Abdullah ibn Salam among you?"" So he sent for them and said: ""What kind of man is Abdullah ibn Salam among you?"" They said: ""He is our best and the son of our best, our scholar and the son of our scholar, and the most knowledgeable among us."" He said: ""What do you think if he were to become Muslim, would you become Muslim?"" They said: ""May Allah protect him from that!"" Then Ibn Salam came out and said: ""I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah."" They said: ""He is our worst and the son of our worst, our ignorant one and the son of our ignorant one."" So he said: ""Ibn Salam, this is what I feared from them."""
"2613","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Years will come upon the people, treacherous years in which the liar is believed and the truthful is called a liar, the traitor is trusted and the trustworthy is accused of betrayal, and the Ruwaybidah will speak. It was said: And what is the Ruwaybidah? He said: The insignificant man in matters of public concern."
"2614","[AI-translation] Abu Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: ""My Ummah will be afflicted with the disease of the nations."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah! What is the disease of the nations?"" He said: ""Recklessness, insolence, vying in worldly increase, and mutual hatred and envy until there is transgression."
"2615","[AI-translation] Aas said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: There will be at the end of my Ummah men riding on saddles resembling the backs of mounts, alighting at the doors of the mosques. Their women will be clothed yet naked, on their heads like the humps of lean camels. Curse them, for they are accursed. Were there behind you a nation from among the nations, your women would serve them just as the women of the nations before you served you."
"2616","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, raised to the Prophet: There will be in the latter times people sitting in the mosques in circles, their aim being this world. Do not sit with them, for Allah has no need of them."
"2617","[AI-translation] Narrated from Nawwas ibn Sam'an, raised to the Prophet: The people will use the bows, arrows, and shields of Ya'juj and Ma'juj as fuel for seven years."
"2618","[AI-translation] Abu Umamah narrated from the Prophet, peace be upon him, that he said: Two groups of my Ummah shall not attain my intercession: an unjust, oppressive imam, and every extremist deviant."
"2619","[AI-translation] Rahman ibn Abi Layla from his father from his grandfather, raised to the Prophet: Two groups of my Ummah will not come to my Hawd: the Qadariyyah and the Murji'ah."
"2620","[AI-translation] Aas said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and said: What is the Sur? He said: The Sur is a horn that is blown into."
"2621","[AI-translation] Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: The molar tooth of the disbeliever on the Day of Resurrection will be like Mount Uhud, and the width of his skin will be seventy cubits, his upper arm like al-Bayda, his thigh like Warqan, and his seat in the Fire will be the distance between me and al-Rabadhah."
"2622","[AI-translation] Umm Salamah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, woke from his sleep repeating the words of Istirja'. I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! What is the matter with you?"" He said: ""A group of my Ummah will be swallowed by the earth, then they will be sent against a man who will come to Makkah, and Allah will protect him from them. They will be swallowed up; their place of death is one, but their origins are diverse. Among them are those who are coerced, so they will come coerced."
"2623","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: Tuba for a life after the Messiah, Tuba for a life after the Messiah. The sky will be permitted to pour down rain, and the earth permitted to bring forth vegetation, such that if you were to plant your seed on al-Safa, it would grow. There will be no contention, no envy, and no mutual hatred, until a man passes by a lion and it does not harm him, and steps on a snake and it does not harm him. There will be no contention, no envy, and no mutual hatred."
"2624","[AI-translation] On the authority of Anas ibn Malik, marfu': The days were presented to me, and among them Friday was presented to me. Thereupon it was like a white mirror, and in its center was a black spot. I asked: ""What is this?"" It was said: ""The Hour."
"2625","[AI-translation] From Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: The punishment of this Ummah is by the sword."
"2626","[AI-translation] From Hudhayfah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) was asked about the Hour, so he said: ""Its knowledge is with my Lord. None reveals its time except Him (Al-A'raf). But I will inform you of its portents and what will precede it. Indeed, preceding it will be: trial and killing."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah! We know the trial, so what is the killing?"" He said: ""In the language of the Abyssinians, it is killing. And mutual estrangement will be cast among the people, such that hardly anyone will recognize anyone."
"2627","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Trials will envelop you like the pieces of a dark night. The safest of people in it will be a man in possession of mountain sheep, who eats from the milk of his sheep, or a man holding the reins of his horse behind the mountain pass, who eats by his sword."
"2628","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), who said: Today, from the barrier of Ya'juj and Ma'juj, an opening like this was made. And Wahb formed ninety with his fingers (and closed them)."
"2629","Abdullah ibn Umar said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah mentioning the tribulations, and he spoke of them extensively until he mentioned the Tribulation of al-Ahlas. A man said: ""O Messenger of Allah, what is the Tribulation of al-Ahlas?"" He said: ""The Tribulation of al-Ahlas is a tribulation of fleeing and war. Then the Tribulation of al-Sarra'—its smoke (or entry) comes from beneath the feet of a man from my household who claims to be from me but is not from me; my allies are only the God-fearing. Then the people will agree upon a man like a hip joint on a rib. Then the Tribulation of al-Duhayma' will not leave anyone from this Ummah except it strikes him a blow. When it is said: 'It has ended,' it will prolong. A man will wake up in it a believer and evening a disbeliever, until the people split into two camps: a camp of faith with no hypocrisy in it, and a camp of hypocrisy with no faith in it. When that occurs, await the Dajjal that day or the next."""
"2630","[AI-translation] From Hudhayfah, that the Prophet of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: In my Ummah there are liars and Dajjals, twenty-seven of them; among them are four women. And I am the seal of the prophets, there is no prophet after me."
"2631","Hudhayfah ibn al-Yamān (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The people used to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) about the good, but I used to ask him about the evil out of fear that it might overtake me. So I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! We were in ignorance (Jāhiliyyah) and evil, then Allah brought us this good (and we are in it) (and He brought you). So is there any evil after this good (just as there was before it)?"" He said: ""O Hudhayfah! Learn the Book of Allah and follow what is in it"" (three times). I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Is there any good after this evil?"" He said: ""Yes."" I said: ""And what is the protection from it?"" He said: ""The sword."" I said: ""And is there any evil after that good?"" (And in another narration: I said: ""And is there any remnant after this sword?"") He said: ""Yes, and in it (and in another narration: there will be an emirate (and in another wording: a community/group) upon spears/bitterness and a truce upon) smoke/dregs (Dukhan)."" I said: ""And what is its smoke/dregs?"" He said: ""A people (and in another narration: there will be after me Imams (who follow other than my Sunnah and) guide with other than my guidance; you will recognize some of their actions and deny others. And there will stand among them men whose hearts are the hearts of devils in the bodies of humans). (And in another narration: The truce upon smoke/dregs—what is it? He said: The hearts of a people do not return to what they were upon)."" I said: ""So is there any evil after that good?"" He said: ""Yes (a blind and deaf fitnah/trial, upon it) are callers at the gates of Hell; whoever answers them to it, they will throw him into it."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Describe them to us."" He said: ""They are from our skin and speak with our tongues."" I said: ""(O Messenger of Allah!) So what do you command me if I reach that (time)?"" He said: ""Adhere to the Jamā'ah (main body) of the Muslims and their Imām (listen and obey the Amīr even if your back is struck and your wealth is taken, so listen and obey)."" I said: ""What if they have no Jamā'ah and no Imām?"" He said: ""Then withdraw from all those sects entirely, even if you have to bite onto the root of a tree until death reaches you while you are upon that. (And in another narration) So if you die, O Hudhayfah, while you are biting onto a stump, that is better for you than following any of them. (And in another) So if you see on that day a Khalīfah of Allah—Mighty and Majestic—on the earth, then adhere to him even if he strikes your back and takes your wealth. But if you do not see a Khalīfah, then flee (in the earth) until death reaches you while you are biting onto the stump of a tree."" (He said: I said: ""Then what?"" He said: ""Then the Dajjāl emerges."" I said: ""With what does he come?"" He said: ""With a river, or he said: water and fire. So whoever enters his river, his reward is nullified and his sin is obligated, and whoever enters his fire, his reward is obligated and his sin is nullified."" (I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Then what is after the Dajjāl?"" He said: ""ʿĪsā ibn Maryam."") He said: I said: ""Then what?"" He said: ""If you were to breed a horse, you would not ride its foal until the Hour is established."""
"2632","On the authority of Salamah ibn Nufayl al-Kindi, he said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) when a man said: ""O Messenger of Allah! The people have abandoned the horses and laid down their weapons, and they said: 'There is no jihad, the war has laid down its burdens.'"" So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) turned his face toward him and said: ""They have lied. Now, now the fighting has come. And there will not cease to be a group from my Ummah fighting upon the truth, and Allah will cause the hearts of some people to deviate for them, and He will provide for them from them, until the Hour is established and until the promise of Allah comes. And goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection. And it has been revealed to me: 'Indeed, I will take you (in death) without delay, and you will follow me in groups, striking the necks of one another, and the abode of the believers is in Sham.'"""
"2633","[AI-translation] From Abu Qabil who said: We were with Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, and he was asked: ""Which of the two cities will be conquered first, Constantinople or Rome?"" So Abdullah called for a box of his with a lock, and he took a book out of it. He said: Abdullah said, ""While we were around the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) writing, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was asked: 'Which of the two cities will be conquered first, Constantinople or Rome?' The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: 'The city of Heraclius will be conquered first,' meaning Constantinople."
"2634","On the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās: A questioner asked him, saying, ""O Abū al-ʿAbbās! Is there any repentance for a murderer?"" Ibn ʿAbbās replied, as if astonished at his affair: ""What do you say?"" The man repeated his question to him, so he said to him: ""What do you say?"" two or three times. Then Ibn ʿAbbās said: ""How can he have repentance? I heard your Prophet ﷺ say: 'The murdered person will come on the Day of Resurrection holding his head in one hand, clutching his murderer with the other hand, his jugular veins gushing with blood, until he comes with him to the Throne. The murdered person will say to the Lord of the Worlds: ""This one killed me."" So Allah will say to the murderer: ""You are doomed,"" and he will be dragged off to the Fire.'"""
"2635","[AI-translation] From Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to me: ""O Shaddad ibn Aws, when you see the people hoarding gold and silver, then increase in these words: O Allah! I ask You for steadfastness in the affair, and determination upon guidance, and I ask You for the necessitors of Your mercy, and the determinations of Your forgiveness, and I ask You for gratitude for Your favor, and excellence in worshipping You, and I ask You for a sound heart, and a truthful tongue, and I ask You for the best of what You know, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You know, and I seek Your forgiveness for what You know. Indeed, You are the Knower of the Unseen."
"2636","[AI-translation] From Aishah, she said: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! When Allah sends down His might upon the people of the earth and there are righteous people among them, do they perish with them?"" He said: ""O Aishah! When Allah sends down His might upon the people of His wrath and there are righteous people among them, they are afflicted along with them, then they are resurrected according to their intentions (and their deeds)."
"2637","[AI-translation] From Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) mentioned a severe hardship that will occur before the Dajjal. She said: I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Where will the Arabs be on that day?"" He said: ""O Aishah! The Arabs on that day will be few."" She said: I asked, ""What will suffice the believers on that day for food?"" He said: ""What suffices the angels: glorification (tasbih), magnification (takbir), praise (tahmid), and declaration of oneness (tahlil)."" She said: I asked, ""Which wealth will be best on that day?"" He said: ""A strong youth who gives his family water to drink, and as for food, there is no food."
"2638","On the authority of Ibn Abbas: ""I was taught a verse from the Quran that no man has ever asked me about, so I do not know whether the people knew it and therefore did not ask about it, or whether they did not perceive it so as to ask about it."" Then he began to narrate to us. When he stood up [to leave], we blamed one another for not having asked him about it! I said: ""I will ask him about it when he comes tomorrow."" When he came the next day, I said: ""O Ibn Abbas! You mentioned yesterday that there is a verse from the Quran that no man has ever asked you about, and you do not know whether the people knew it so they did not ask, or they did not perceive it. So inform me about it and about the verses you recited before it."" He said: ""Yes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Quraysh: 'O assembly of Quraysh! There is none worshipped besides Allah in whom there is any good.' And Quraysh knew that the Christians worship Jesus son of Mary, so what do you say about Muhammad? They said: 'O Muhammad! Do you not claim that Jesus was a Prophet and a righteous servant from the servants of Allah?! If you are truthful, then their gods are as they say (the original text has: 'as you say!').' So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: 'And when the son of Mary is presented as an example, behold, your people therefrom raise a clamor' (Az-Zukhruf: 57). I said: 'What is (yasidduun)?' He said: 'They clamor/noisily object.' 'And indeed, he is knowledge for the Hour' (Az-Zukhruf: 61). He said: 'It is the descent of Jesus son of Mary, peace be upon him, before the Day of Resurrection.'"""
"2639","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah from Abu Qatadah that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""A man will be pledged allegiance between the Rukn and the Maqam, and the House will not be profaned except by its own people. When they profane it, do not ask about the destruction of the Arabs. Then the Abyssinians will come and destroy it with a destruction such that it will never be inhabited after it, and they are the ones who will extract its treasure."
"2640","[AI-translation] Narrated Said ibn Samaan who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah informing Abu Qatadah that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""A man will be pledged allegiance between the Rukn and the Maqam, and the House will not be profaned except by its own people. When they profane it, one will not be asked about the destruction of the Arabs. Then the Abyssinians will come and destroy it with a destruction such that it will never be inhabited after it, and they are the ones who will extract its treasure."
"2641","[AI-translation] Narrated Sawdah, the wife of the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Mankind will be resurrected barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised. The sweat will gag them and reach the cartilage of the ears."" Sawdah said: ""I said: O Messenger of Allah! How awful! Will some of us look at others?"" He said: ""Mankind will be preoccupied from that."" And he recited: ""The Day a man will flee from his brother (34), and his mother and his father (35), and his wife and his sons (36). For every man among them that Day will be a matter sufficient for him (37)"" (Abasa)."
"2642","[AI-translation] Narrated Kab ibn Malik, marfu: ""Mankind will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection, and I and my Ummah will be upon a hill. My Lord will clothe me in a green garment, then permission will be given to me, and I will say whatever Allah wills for me to say. That is the Praised Station."
"2643","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Seventy thousand from the Jews of Isfahan will follow the Dajjal, wearing shawls."
"2644","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Musa who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Our Lord, Mighty and Majestic, will manifest Himself to us on the Day of Resurrection, laughing."
"2645","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, saying: ""They will leave Madinah in the best condition it was; none will enter it except the beasts of prey (he meant: the beasts of prey and birds). The last to be gathered will be two shepherds from Muzaynah heading towards Madinah, calling their sheep. They will find it a wilderness until, when they reach Thaniyyat al-Wada, they will fall on their faces."
"2646","On the authority of Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, traced back to the Prophet ﷺ: The Prophet comes accompanied by two men, and a prophet comes accompanied by three, and more than that, and fewer. It is then said to him: ""Did you convey the message to your people?"" He replies: ""Yes."" Then his people are summoned and it is asked: ""Did this one convey the message to you?"" They say: ""No."" It is said: ""Who will bear witness for you?"" He says: ""Muḥammad ﷺ and his nation."" So the nation of Muḥammad is summoned and it is asked: ""Did he convey the message?"" They say: ""Yes."" It is said: ""And what is your knowledge of that?"" They say: ""Our Prophet informed us that the messengers had conveyed the message, so we believed him."" That is the meaning of His saying, Exalted is He: {And thus We have made you a just community that you will be witnesses over the people and the Messenger will be a witness over you} (Al-Baqarah: 143)."
"2647","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: ""Mankind will be gathered on three paths: eager, fearful, two on a camel, three on a camel, four on a camel, and ten on a camel. The Fire will gather the rest of them, resting with them at midday where they rested at midday, spending the night with them where they spent the night, arriving in the morning with them where they arrived in the morning, and arriving in the evening with them where they arrived in the evening."
"2648","[AI-translation] Narrated Said ibn Amr who said: Abdullah ibn Amr came to Ibn al-Zubayr while he was sitting in the Hijr and said: ""O Ibn al-Zubayr! Beware of deviation in the Sanctuary of Allah, for I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, saying: 'A man from Quraysh will violate its sanctity, and he will be destroyed by it. If his sins were weighed against the sins of the Thaqalayn, they would outweigh them.' He (Ibn al-Zubayr) said: 'See that you are not him, O Ibn Amr! For you have read the books and accompanied the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family.' He (Abdullah ibn Amr) said: 'So I make you witness that my face is towards Sham, as a mujahid.'"
"2649","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Said that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""The Mahdi will emerge at the end of my Ummah. Allah will give him rain, the earth will bring forth its vegetation, he will give wealth in full, livestock will increase, and the Ummah will grow great. He will live for seven or eight, meaning Hajj (pilgrimages)."
"2650","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Twelve thousand will emerge from Aden Abyan, helping Allah and His Messenger. They are the best of those between me and them."
"2651","On the authority of Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān, marfūʿ (attributed to the Prophet ﷺ): “Islam will wear away just as the embroidery of a garment wears away, until no one will know what fasting is, nor prayer, nor rites of pilgrimage, nor charity. And the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will be taken away in a single night, so that not a single verse of it will remain on the earth. And groups of people will remain: the old man and the old woman, saying: ‘We found our fathers upon this statement: “There is no deity but Allah,” so we say it.’ Ṣilah ibn Zafr said to Ḥudhayfah: ‘What will “There is no deity but Allah” avail them when they do not know what prayer is, nor fasting, nor rites of pilgrimage, nor charity?’ Ḥudhayfah turned away from him. Then he repeated it to him three times, each time Ḥudhayfah turning away from him. Then he turned to him on the third time and said: ‘O Ṣilah! It will save them from the Fire,’ three times.”"
"2652","[AI-translation] Aslami: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""The righteous will pass away, the foremost and the foremost, and there will remain a residue like the residue of barley or dates; Allah will not care for them at all."
"2653","[AI-translation] Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""This religion will prevail until it crosses the seas, and until horses are ridden in the cause of Allah. Then a people will come who recite the Quran. When they recite it, they will say: 'We have recited the Quran; so who is a better reciter than us? Who is more knowledgeable than us?' Then he turned to his companions and said: 'Do you see any good in them?' They replied: 'No.' He said: 'They are from among you, from this nation, and they are the fuel of the Fire.'"
"2654","On the authority of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Ya'juj and Ma'juj (Gog and Magog) will be let loose and they will surge upon the people, as Allah the Mighty and Majestic said: 'From every mound they will swarm forth' (Al-Anbiya: 96). They will cover the earth, and the Muslims will withdraw from them into their cities and strongholds, and they will bring their livestock with them. They will drink the waters of the earth until one of them passes by a river and drinks what is in it until they leave it dry, until one who comes after them passes by that river and says: 'There used to be water here once!' Until when none of the people remain except one in a fortress or a city, their leader will say: 'These are the people of the earth; we have finished them off. Now remain the people of the heaven.' Then one of them will shake his spear and hurl it toward the sky, and it will return stained with blood as a trial and tribulation. While they are in that state, Allah will send worms into their necks like the worms that emerge from the necks of locusts, and they will become dead, with no sound heard from them. The Muslims will say: 'Is there not a man who will sacrifice himself to see what this enemy has done?' So a man from them will volunteer for that, seeking reward for himself, thinking that he will be killed. He will descend and find them dead, piled upon one another. He will call out: 'O company of Muslims! Rejoice, for Allah has sufficed you against your enemy!' They will come out from their cities and strongholds and let their livestock loose, but they will find no pasture for them except their flesh. They will fatten on it as the best they have ever fattened on any vegetation they ever chanced upon."""
"2655","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""The creation will exact retribution from one another, even the hornless sheep from the horned one, and even the ant from the ant."
"2656","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah, raised to the Prophet: Allah will judge between His creation—the jinn, humans, and beasts—and on that Day He will exact retribution for the hornless sheep from the horned one, until when no claim remains for anyone against another, Allah will say: ""Be dust."" At that, the disbeliever will say: ""If only I were dust!"" (An-Nisa: 40)"
"2657","On the authority of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, marfu': Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say on the Day of Resurrection: ""O Adam!"" He will say: ""Here I am, our Lord, and at Your service!"" Then a voice will call out: ""Indeed Allah commands you to bring forth from your offspring a batch for the Fire."" He will say: ""O Lord! And what is the batch for the Fire?"" He will say: ""From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine."" At that time, the pregnant woman will drop her load, and the child will turn gray-haired, (and you will see the people as if they are drunk, but they are not drunk; rather, the punishment of Allah is severe) [Al-Hajj: 2]. This will be so distressing to the people that their faces will change. The Prophet ﷺ said: ""From Gog and Magog, nine hundred and ninety-nine, and from you, one."" Then you are among the people like a black hair on the side of a white bull, or like a white hair on the side of a black bull. And I hope that you will be one-fourth of the people of Paradise."" So we said Allahu Akbar. Then he said: ""One-third of the people of Paradise."" So we said Allahu Akbar. Then he said: ""Half of the people of Paradise."" So we said Allahu Akbar."
"2658","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Said: I heard the Prophet (peace be upon him) say: ""Our Lord will uncover His Shin, and every believing man and woman will prostrate to Him. But there will remain everyone who used to prostrate in the world out of showing off and seeking reputation; he will go to prostrate, but his back will become a single flat sheet."
"2659","From Abu Nadrah, who said: We were with Jabir ibn Abdullah when he said: ""The people of Iraq will soon have no qafiz nor dirham brought to them."" We said: ""From where will that be?"" He said: ""From the direction of the non-Arabs, who will prevent that."" Then he said: ""The people of Syria will soon have no dinar nor mudd brought to them."" We said: ""From where will that be?"" He said: ""From the direction of the Romans."" Then he fell silent for a moment, then said: ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There will be in the last of my Ummah a Caliph who will scatter wealth profusely, not counting it.'"" He said: I said to Abu Nadrah and Abu al-Ala: ""Do you two think that it is Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz?"" They both said: ""No."""
"2660","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Umamah, raised to the Prophet: ""In the end of times, there will be men in this nation who will have whips like the tails of cows. They will go out in the morning in Allah's wrath and return in the evening in His anger."
"2661","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir bin Samurah, raised to the Prophet: ""After me there will be twelve princes, all of them from Quraysh."
"2662","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Isa bin Maryam will descend, and their leader, the Mahdi, will say: 'Come, lead us in prayer.' He will say: 'No; some of you are leaders over others, as an honor from Allah to this nation.'"
"2663","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Umar: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: ""A generation will arise who will recite the Quran, but it will not go beyond their collarbones. Every time a generation emerges, it will be cut off, until the Dajjal emerges in their midst."
"2664","[AI-translation] From Thawban, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""The nations will soon call one another against you just as eaters call one another to their bowl."" Someone asked: ""Will it be because of our small number on that day?"" He said: ""No, you will be many on that day, but you will be scum like the scum of the flood. And Allah will surely remove the awe of you from the chests of your enemy, and Allah will surely cast al-wahn into your hearts."" Someone asked: ""O Messenger of Allah! What is al-wahn?"" He said: ""Love of the world and hatred of death."
"2665","[AI-translation] 'Abdullah said (as a statement traced to him): ""You will soon seek a basin of water in these villages of yours but will not find it. All water will retreat to its origin, and the remainder of the believers and the water will be in Al-Sham."
"2666","[AI-translation] From a man among the Companions of the Prophet, peace be upon him, from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, who said: ""A lowly son of a lowly man will soon prevail over the world, and the best of people is a believer between two noble ones."
"2667","[AI-translation] Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, who said: 'Abdullah ibn Wuzaj had an early companionship, and he narrated to us that the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""A weak man will soon be appointed over them, and a people will gather to him with shaved necks and white garments, and whenever he commands them to do something, they will carry it out."" And your Lord willed that 'Abdullah ibn Wuzaj be appointed over a city, and a group of the Dahaqin (landowners) gathered to him, with shaved necks and white garments, and whenever he commanded them to do something, they would carry it out. He would say: ""Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth."
"2668","Mu'adh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: We went out with Allah's Messenger (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) in the year of the Tabuk expedition. He would combine the prayers, so he prayed Zuhr and 'Asr together, and Maghrib and 'Isha' together. Until one day he delayed the prayer, then went out and prayed Zuhr and 'Asr together, then entered, then went out after that and prayed Maghrib and 'Isha' together. Then he said: ""You will come tomorrow, if Allah wills, to the spring of Tabuk, and you will not reach it until midday. So whoever of you reaches it, let him not touch any of its water until I come."" So we came to it, and two men had preceded us to it. The spring was like a shoelace, trickling with a little water. Allah's Messenger (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) asked them: ""Did you touch any of its water?"" They said: ""Yes."" The Prophet (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) cursed them and said to them what Allah willed him to say. Then they scooped up water from the spring with their hands, little by little, until it collected in a vessel. He said: And Allah's Messenger (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) washed his hands and face in it, then poured it back into it. The spring gushed forth with abundant water (or he said: copious water) until the people had their fill. Then he said: ""Soon, O Mu'adh, if you live long enough, you will see this place filled with gardens."""
"2669","[AI-translation] From Salman, from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: ""The Scale will be placed on the Day of Resurrection, and if the heavens and the earth were weighed in it, it would accommodate them. The angels will say: 'O Lord! For whom is this weighed?' Allah, Exalted be He, will say: 'For whomsoever I will of My creation.' The angels will say: 'Glory be to You! We have not worshipped You with the true right of Your worship.' And the Bridge (al-Sirat) will be laid down like the edge of a sword. The angels will say: 'Who will cross over this?' He will say: 'Whomsoever I will of My creation.' They will say: 'Glory be to You! We have not worshipped You with the true right of Your worship.'"
"2670","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, who said: ""The Day of Resurrection is the length of what is between Dhuhr and 'Asr."
"2671","[AI-translation] He, peace be upon him, said: ""How can I be at ease when the one entrusted with the horn has placed it to his mouth, lowered his forehead, and inclined his ear, waiting to be commanded to blow, and so he blows?"" The Muslims said: ""What should we say then, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""Say: 'Allah is Sufficient for us and the Best Disposer of affairs. We have placed our trust in Allah, our Lord.'"" And Sufyan sometimes said: ""In Allah we have placed our trust."" It was narrated in the hadith of... and al-Bara' ibn 'Aazib, may Allah be pleased with them."
"2672","[AI-translation] 'As, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, recited the verse: ""The Day when mankind will stand before the Lord of the worlds"" [Al-Mutaffifin: 6], and the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""How will it be for you when Allah gathers you just as arrows are gathered in a quiver for fifty thousand years, and then Allah will not look at you?"
"2673","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""How will it be for you, O 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, when you are left among the dregs of people whose covenants and trusts have become corrupted, and they have differed, becoming like this?"" And he intertwined his fingers. He said: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! What do you command me?"" He said: ""Cling to your private affairs, and leave their common folk alone."
"2674","[AI-translation] From Hudhayfah, who said: The Dajjal was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, and he said: ""I am more fearful for you of the tribulation caused by some of you than the tribulation of the Dajjal. And no one will be saved from what precedes it except he who is saved from it. No tribulation has been wrought since the world began, be it small or great, except for the tribulation of the Dajjal."
"2675","On the authority of Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad, who said: I witnessed Ali and al-Zubayr when al-Zubayr returned on his mount, cutting through the ranks. His son Abdullah intercepted him and said: ""What is the matter with you?"" He said: ""Ali mentioned to me a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'You will fight him while you are in the wrong.' So I will not fight him."" He said: ""Did you come to fight? You only came to reconcile between people, and Allah will set right this matter through you."" He said: ""I have sworn not to fight."" He said: ""Then free your slave Jirjis and stay until you reconcile between people."" So he freed his slave Jirjis and stayed, but the people's affair became disordered, so he departed on his horse."
"2676","[AI-translation] From Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""There will surely come upon my Ummah a time when they will wish for the Dajjal."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you! From what is that?"" He said: ""From the hardship or distress they will face."
"2677","[AI-translation] From Aishah or Umm Salamah, that the Prophet, peace be upon him, said to one of them: An angel entered upon me in the house, one who had never entered upon me before her. He said to me: ""This son of yours, Husayn, will be killed, and if you wish, I will show you the dust of the earth where he will be killed."" He said: So he brought out red dust."
"2678","[AI-translation] Zubayr, he said: I asked Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, about the arriving? So he informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: ""We, on the Day of Resurrection, will be upon a hill above the people, the nations with their idols and what the first ones used to worship. Then our Lord will come to us after that and say: 'What are you waiting for?' They will say: 'We are waiting for our Lord.' He will say: 'I am your Lord.' They will say: 'Until we look at You.' So He will manifest Himself to them, laughing, and they will follow Him."
"2679","[AI-translation] Sa'd said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: ""What a good death it is that a man dies for his right."
"2680","Jabir ibn Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) overlooked a mountain pass of the mountain passes of Al-Harrah while we were with him, and he said: ""Excellent is the land of Al-Madinah. When the Dajjal emerges, at every mountain pass of its mountain passes there will be an angel who will not enter it. So when that happens, Al-Madinah will shake with its people three tremors. No hypocrite man or woman will remain but will go out to him."" And most of those who go out to him are women. ""And that is the Day of Purification, and that is the day Al-Madinah expels its impurities just as the bellows expels the impurities of iron. With him will be seventy thousand Jews, each wearing a turban and a curved sword. Their necks will be struck with this strike at the place where the torrents meet.""Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""There has never been a fitnah (trial/tribulation) and there will never be one until the Hour is established greater than the fitnah of the Dajjal. And no prophet but warned his nation of him. And I will inform you of something no prophet before me informed his nation."" Then he placed his hand on his eyes and said: ""I bear witness that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is not one-eyed."""
"2681","[AI-translation] From Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""Do you have any Anmat?"" I said: ""And how would we have Anmat?!"" He said: ""Verily, you will have Anmat."" Jabir said: So I say to her, meaning his wife, ""Keep your Anmat away from us,"" and she says, ""Did the Prophet, peace be upon him, not say: 'You will have Anmat'?!"" So I leave it."
"2682","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: ""By Him in Whose hand is the soul of Abu al-Qasim, Isa son of Maryam will surely descend as a just Imam and a fair judge. He will break the cross, kill the pig, reconcile relations, remove enmity, and wealth will be presented to him but he will not accept it. Then, if he stands by my grave and says: 'O Muhammad', I will answer him."
"2683","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet, peace be upon him, went out to a group of his companions who were laughing and talking, and he said: ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul! If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."" Then he left and made the people weep, and Allah revealed to him: ""O Muhammad! Why do you cause My servants to despair?"" So the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, returned and said: ""Rejoice, and be straight and draw near."
"2684","Abu Bakrah narrated that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by a man prostrating while he was on his way to the prayer. He performed the prayer and returned to him while he was still prostrating. The Prophet stood up and said: ""Who will kill this man?"" A man stood up, rolled up his sleeves, drew his sword and brandished it, then said: ""O Messenger of Allah! May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, how can I kill a man who is prostrating and testifies that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger?"" Then he said: ""Who will kill this man?"" A man stood up and said: ""I will."" He rolled up his sleeves, drew his sword and brandished it until his hand trembled, then said: ""O Messenger of Allah! How can I kill a man who is prostrating and testifies that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger?"" The Prophet said: ""By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, if you had killed him, it would have been the first fitnah and the last of it."""
"2685","On the authority of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: A wolf attacked a sheep and took it. The shepherd pursued it and rescued it from him. The wolf sat on its tail and said: ""Do you not fear Allah? You snatch from me a provision that Allah has sent to me?"" The shepherd said: ""How amazing! A wolf sitting on its tail speaking to me with human speech?"" The wolf said: ""Shall I not inform you of something more amazing than that? Muhammad (peace be upon him) in Yathrib informing people of the news of what has passed."" So the shepherd drove his sheep until he entered the city, confined them in a corner of its corners, then came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and informed him. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) ordered the call to be made: ""The prayer is a gathering."" Then he went out and said to the shepherd: ""Inform them."" So he informed them. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""He has spoken the truth, and by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, the Hour will not be established until beasts speak to humans, and a man's whip strap and his sandal strap speak to him, and his thigh informs him of what his family did after him."""
"2686","[AI-translation] Ash'ari, he heard the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, say: ""There will surely be among my Ummah people who will make lawful the private parts, silk, wine, and musical instruments. And there will surely be people who camp by the side of a mountain, and a shepherd will come to them in the evening with their grazing animals, coming to them for a need, and they will say: 'Come back to us tomorrow.' So Allah will destroy them overnight, and remove the mountain, and transform others into monkeys and pigs until the Day of Resurrection."
"2687","[AI-translation] From Umm Habibah, from Zaynab bint Jahsh, the wife of the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, came out to us one day alarmed, his face red, saying: ""There is no god but Allah! Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near! Today an opening has been made in the barrier of Ya'juj and Ma'juj like this,"" and he made a ring with his thumb and the finger next to it. She said: I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Will we be destroyed while the righteous are among us?"" He said: ""Yes, when wickedness abounds."
"2688","[AI-translation] From Imran ibn Husayn, raised to the Prophet: ""A group from my Ummah will remain manifest upon the truth until the Hour is established."
"2689","From Abdur-Rahman ibn Shimasah al-Mahri, he said: I was with Maslamah ibn Mukhallad, and with him was Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As. Abdullah said: ""The Hour will not be established except upon the worst of creation; they are worse than the people of the pre-Islamic ignorance. They do not call upon Allah for anything except that He rejects them."" While they were in that state, Uqbah ibn Amir approached. Maslamah said to him: ""O Uqbah! Listen to what Abdullah is saying."" Uqbah said: ""He knows better. As for me, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: 'A group from my Ummah will continue to fight for the cause of Allah, prevailing over their enemies. Those who oppose them will not harm them until the Hour comes upon them while they are in that state.'"" Abdullah said: ""Yes. Then Allah will send a wind like the wind of musk, its touch like the touch of silk. It will not leave any person in whose heart is faith the weight of a mustard seed except that it takes his soul. Then the worst of people will remain, and upon them the Hour will be established."""
"2690","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Mas'ud from the Prophet (peace be upon him) who said: The foot of the son of Adam will not move on the Day of Resurrection from before his Lord until he is asked about five: about his life, in what he consumed it; about his youth, in what he exhausted it; about his wealth, from where he acquired it; and in what he spent it; and what he did with what he knew."
"2691","[AI-translation] Harith b. Malik Ibn Barsa' (marfu'an): This (meaning Mecca) will not be invaded after today until the Day of Resurrection. (And no Qurashi will ever be killed in cold blood after this year)."
"2692","[AI-translation] Narrated Samura who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: The Hour will not be established until the mountains depart from their places, and you see great matters that you did not use to see."
"2693","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Juhayfa who said: I burped in the presence of the Prophet (peace be upon him), so he said: What did you eat, O Abu Juhayfa? I said: Bread and meat. He said: The people who will suffer hunger the longest on the Day of Resurrection are those who were the most satiated in this world."
"2694","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Abbas (marfu'an): Some people from my Ummah will surely recite the Quran, but they will pass out of Islam just as an arrow passes through the game."
"2695","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas (marfu'an): There will surely occur in this Ummah sinking into the earth, pelting, and metamorphosis, and that is when they drink wine, employ female singers, and play musical instruments."
"2696","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Umar (marfu'an): ""Trials will surely encompass my Ummah after me like the pieces of a dark night. A man will become a believer in the morning and a disbeliever by evening, and he will become a believer by evening and a disbeliever in the morning. Some people will sell their religion for a small portion of this world."
"2697","[AI-translation] Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: A group from my Ummah will certainly make wine lawful by a name they will give it (in another narration: they will call it by other than its name)."
"2698","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayra who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Some people will certainly wish that they had committed more evil deeds. They said: By what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Those whose evil deeds Allah has changed into good deeds."
"2699","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Some people of this Ummah will surely spend the night engaged in food, drink, and amusement, and they will wake up having been transformed into monkeys and pigs."
"2700","[AI-translation] From Abu Dharr he said: We set out with the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, and we stopped at Dhu al-Hulayfah. Some men hastened to al-Madinah, and the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, spent the night, and we spent the night with him. When morning came, he asked about them. It was said: They hastened to al-Madinah. He said: They hastened to al-Madinah and to the women. Verily, they will leave it better than it was. Then he said: Would that I knew! When will a fire emerge from Yemen, from Mount al-Wiraq, illuminating the necks of the kneeling camels in Busrā like the light of day."
"2701","[AI-translation] From 'Abd Allah bin 'Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: There will come upon mankind a time when their hearts are the hearts of the 'Ajam. (I said: And what are the hearts of the 'Ajam? He said:) Love of the world. Their way is the way of the A'rab: whatever provision comes to them, they put it into livestock. They view Jihad as a harm, and Zakat as a fine."
"2702","[AI-translation] From a group among them: Al-Miqdad, Abu Tha'labah, and Tamim al-Dari, marfu'an: This matter will certainly reach what the night and day have reached. And Allah will not leave any house of mud or hair except that Allah will enter this religion into it, with the honor of an honored one or the humiliation of a humiliated one. An honor by which Allah honors Islam, and a humiliation by which Allah humiliates disbelief."
"2703","[AI-translation] 'As who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: From the approaching (and in a narration: the signs) of the Hour is that the wicked will be raised and the good will be abased, speech will be opened and action withheld, and the mathanat will be recited among a people with no one among them denouncing it. It was said: And what is the mathanat? He said: What is written other than the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"2704","[AI-translation] From Anas, marfu'an: Whoever among you meets 'Isa son of Maryam, let him convey my peace to him."
"2705","[AI-translation] Zubayr bin 'Adi he said: We entered upon Anas bin Malik and complained to him about what we faced from Al-Hajjaj. He said: He, peace be upon him, said: There is no year except that the one after it is worse than it, until you meet your Lord."
"2706","[AI-translation] From Usamah bin Zayd bin Harithah (and Sa'id bin Zayd bin 'Amr bin Nufayl) from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him: I did not leave behind after me a trial more harmful to men than women."
"2707","[AI-translation] Mazini from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, that he said: There is no one from my Ummah except that I will know him on the Day of Resurrection. They said: And how will you know them, O Messenger of Allah, given the multitude of creations? He said: What do you think, if you entered a corral in which there were jet-black horses, and among them a horse with a blaze and white markings on its legs, would you not recognize it from among them? He said: Yes. He said: Thus, my Ummah on that day will have shining foreheads from prostration and bright marks from ablution."
"2708","Abu al-Aswad al-Dailami said: I went to Imran ibn Husayn one day, and he said: ""O Abu al-Aswad!"" Then he narrated the hadith that a man from Juhaynah or from Muzaynah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! What do you think about what people do today and strive in — is it something that has been decreed upon them and has passed upon them in a divine decree that has preceded, or is it in what they will encounter of what their Prophet ﷺ brought them and the proof was established against them thereby?"" He said: ""Rather, it is something that has been decreed upon them and has passed upon them."" He said: ""Then why do they work, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""Whoever Allah Mighty and Majestic created for one of the two stations, He facilitates him for its deed."" And the confirmation of that is in the Book of Allah Mighty and Majestic: ""And [by] the soul and He who proportioned it (7) And inspired it [with discernment of] its wickedness and its righteousness (8)"" (Ash-Shams: 7-8)."
"2709","[AI-translation] Darda' from the Prophet, peace be upon him, he said: Whoever memorizes ten verses from the beginning of Surat al-Kahf will be protected from (the trial of) the Dajjal."
"2710","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: From the signs of the approaching of the Hour is the swelling of the crescent moons, and that the crescent is seen for one night, so it is said: It is two nights old."
"2711","[AI-translation] From 'Ali, raised to the Prophet: Al-Mahdi is from us, the Ahl al-Bayt. Allah will rectify him in a single night."
"2712","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: Al-Maqam al-Mahmud is the intercession."
"2713","[AI-translation] From Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""From us is the one behind whom 'Isa ibn Maryam will pray."
"2714","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""The Hour will not be established until trials appear, lying becomes widespread, markets draw close, time draws close, and Harj increases."" It was said: ""And what is Harj?"" He said: ""Killing."
"2715","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: The Hour will not be established until the land of the Arabs returns to meadows and rivers."
"2716","[AI-translation] Khudri, raised to the Prophet: The Hour will not be established until you fight a people with small eyes and broad faces, as if their eyes are the pupils of locusts and their faces are like hammered shields. They wear hair as footwear and adopt shields, until they tie their horses to the palm trees."
"2717","[AI-translation] Khudri, raised to the Prophet: The Hour will not be established until the House is no longer visited for Hajj."
"2718","[AI-translation] From Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""The Hour will not be established until a man kills his neighbor, his brother, and his father."
"2719","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""The Hour will not be established until a man passes by the grave of a man and says: 'Would that I were in his place!' not out of love for meeting Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"2720","[AI-translation] From Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""The Hour will not be established until the people are rained upon with a general rain, yet the earth will not sprout anything."
"2721","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: The Hour will not be established until the people are rained upon with a rain from which the houses of clay will not afford shelter, and none will afford shelter from it except the houses of hair."
"2722","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah, raised to the Prophet: The night and the day will not depart until a man from the Mawali rules, who is called Jahjah."
"2723","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: The Hour will not be established until people build houses which they decorate with the decoration of Marahil."
"2724","[AI-translation] Narrated Abdullah bin Amr: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: The Hour will not be established until they copulate in the roads like the copulation of donkeys. I said: ""Will that really happen?"" He said: ""Yes, it will surely happen."
"2725","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family): The expeditions will not cease from attacking this House until an army of theirs is swallowed up."
"2726","[AI-translation] Narrated Aishah, raised to the Prophet: The night and the day will not depart until Al-Lat and Al-Uzza are worshipped. Aishah said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I thought when Allah revealed: 'He it is Who sent His Messenger with guidance and the religion of truth, to make it prevail over all religion, even though the polytheists may detest it' (At-Tawbah: 33), that this would be complete."" He said: ""There will be of that whatever Allah wills."
"2727","[AI-translation] Sahih number: Sahih Muslim, Book of Tribulations and Portents of the Hour, Chapter: The Hour will not be established until Daws worships Dhu al-Khalasah, Number (5174)."
"2728","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Allah will not look on the Day of Resurrection at an old man who commits adultery, nor at an old woman who commits adultery."
"2729","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas, raised to the Prophet: There will come upon the people a time when the one patient upon his religion among them will be like one grasping onto embers."
"2730","[AI-translation] Narrated Maymunah: She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said one day: How will you be when religion is corrupted (and blood is shed, and adornment appears, and buildings are raised), and greed appears, and brothers differ, and the Ancient House is burned?"
"2731","[AI-translation] Narrated from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrat, from his father, raised to the Prophet: The earth will surely be filled with injustice and oppression, and when it is filled with injustice and oppression, Allah will send a man from me whose name is my name, and he will fill it with justice and equity just as it was filled with injustice and oppression."
"2732","[AI-translation] Khushani who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Allah will not abandon this Ummah for half a day."
